          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " dishcloth is 20 x 20 cm. Puffs sit in every other stitch on every other row. The round, soft raised element is gentler on delicate surfaces than a bobble."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "DK cotton on a 4 mm hook. Total yarn needed is around 35 m. Puffs use slightly more yarn than dc because of the extra loops."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What you need"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "suppliesCard",
        "attrs": {
          "heading": "Materials",
          "items": [
            {
              "name": "DK cotton yarn",
              "qty": "35 m (about 28 g)"
            },
            {
              "name": "4 mm crochet hook",
              "qty": "1"
            },
            {
              "name": "Tapestry needle",
              "qty": "1"
            },
            {
              "name": "Scissors",
              "qty": "1 pair"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "How to work a puff"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "*Yarn over, insert hook into stitch, pull up loop*. Repeat 3 times (7 loops on hook). Yarn over and draw through all 7 loops. Ch 1 to close. One puff made."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
